---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="ConfigTrace 1.0.1 | Marcelo Ellwanger" description="ConfigTrace 1.0.1 is a lightweight Rust configuration-change tracer with deterministic snapshots, field-level diffs, sensitive-key redaction, event-driven JSONL journals and a validated CrashScope 1.1 integration boundary.">
  <section class="case-hero case-hero-featured wrap">
    <div class="case-title-block">
      <p class="eyebrow">08 · Focused project · 1.0.1 released · Rust</p>
      <h1>ConfigTrace</h1>
      <p class="case-copy">A standalone configuration-evidence engine that records what actually changed around a game or application session without turning a diagnostic helper into another heavyweight background monitor.</p>
      <div class="case-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/marcelosofficial-ctrl/ConfigTrace/releases/download/v1.0.1/ConfigTrace-1.0.1-win-x64.zip" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Download 1.0.1 ↗</a>
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/marcelosofficial-ctrl/ConfigTrace" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open repository ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="case-status-panel mono" aria-label="ConfigTrace release and resource snapshot">
      <div class="case-status-head"><span>FOCUSED / RELEASE</span><b>1.0.1</b></div>
      <div class="case-status-row"><span>Runtime</span><strong>RUST</strong></div>
      <div class="case-status-row"><span>CrashScope sample · avg WS</span><strong>4.96 MB</strong></div>
      <div class="case-status-row"><span>CrashScope sample · peak WS</span><strong>4.99 MB</strong></div>
      <div class="case-status-row"><span>Measured avg CPU</span><strong>0%</strong></div>
      <div class="case-status-foot"><span class="status-dot">1.0.1 · RELEASED · PRIVACY FIX VALIDATED</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap case-intro-grid">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">The design choice</p><h2>Keep the evidence provider independent from the product consuming it.</h2></div>
    <div class="case-long-copy">
      <p>ConfigTrace is useful on its own and now ships as CrashScope 1.1's first external evidence provider. The integration boundary is process isolation plus schema-versioned JSON/JSONL contracts rather than a direct Rust/C# ABI.</p>
      <p>That keeps lifecycle, failure isolation and versioning explicit: CrashScope can launch ConfigTrace for a monitored session, consume bounded evidence, and stop it without duplicating its parsing logic or letting provider failure take down the host.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap">
    <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Semantic evidence</p><h2>Record meaningful state changes, not raw filesystem noise.</h2></div>
    <div class="model-grid">
      <article><span class="mono model-index">01</span><h3>Deterministic snapshots</h3><p>Regular files receive streamed SHA-256 fingerprints and stable relative paths for repeatable comparison.</p></article>
      <article><span class="mono model-index">02</span><h3>Field-level diffs</h3><p>JSON and common INI/CFG-style files expose structured value changes instead of only whole-file hashes.</p></article>
      <article><span class="mono model-index">03</span><h3>Privacy-aware redaction</h3><p>Version 1.0.1 fixes sensitive-key recognition for camelCase/PascalCase values such as apiToken, accessToken, clientSecret, sessionId and APIKey while keeping change fingerprints useful.</p></article>
      <article><span class="mono model-index">04</span><h3>Event-driven journal</h3><p>Native filesystem notifications wake the watcher, then a settle window and semantic resnapshot turn noisy writes into stable JSONL change records.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap">
    <div class="field-grid">
      <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Validated integration overhead</p><h2>Small enough to stay a sidecar.</h2><p>These figures come from CrashScope 1.1's final active provider validation sample, not a universal performance claim.</p></div>
      <div class="field-console mono">
        <div><span>measured average CPU</span><b>0%</b></div>
        <div><span>average working set</span><b>4.96 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>peak working set</span><b>4.99 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>average private memory</span><b>0.91 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>provider journal</span><b>PASS</b></div>
        <div><span>plaintext test secret</span><b>NOT FOUND</b></div>
        <div><span>validated commit</span><b>b629c970</b></div>
        <div class="field-result"><span>release state</span><strong>RELEASED 1.0.1</strong></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap">
    <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">CrashScope boundary</p><h2>Correlation evidence, never automatic causation.</h2></div>
    <div class="case-long-copy">
      <p>CrashScope 1.1 can report that HDR, renderer or another configuration field changed a measured amount of time before an incident. ConfigTrace alone does not justify claiming that the change caused the incident.</p>
      <p>The schema-v1 snapshot/diff and live-journal contracts remain the stable integration boundary used by CrashScope 1.1, while ConfigTrace stays independently usable as a standalone utility.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap">
    <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Release provenance</p><h2>A small maintenance release with a concrete reason.</h2></div>
    <div class="skill-matrix">
      <div><span>Validated commit</span><p><code>b629c970dfc14fca5df1e0ef2b0d1d07d0d8c56c</code></p></div>
      <div><span>Windows EXE SHA-256</span><p><code>fe1c470a58402e82e97ee529c6a6b02822430da70e65ffc5fc5a71359ad4e521</code></p></div>
      <div><span>Release ZIP SHA-256</span><p><code>9374128c42e3bf3e1fd8f48bdddd7485e421da543c80f54d454985e1bcccbafe</code></p></div>
      <div><span>1.0.1 change</span><p>Fix camelCase sensitive-key redaction discovered during CrashScope 1.1 integration.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section case-closing wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Focused utility · 1.0.1</p>
    <h2>A tiny Rust process with a deliberately stable boundary.</h2>
    <p>ConfigTrace shows systems work at a small scale: filesystem events, deterministic state, privacy constraints, integration contracts, measured resource use and a maintenance release driven by a real integration finding.</p>
    <div class="case-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/marcelosofficial-ctrl/ConfigTrace/releases/download/v1.0.1/ConfigTrace-1.0.1-win-x64.zip" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Download 1.0.1 ↗</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/marcelosofficial-ctrl/ConfigTrace" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View source ↗</a>
      <a class="button" href="/">Back to portfolio ↑</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>